- `src-tauri/src/notifications.rs` -- the device half of the encrypted notification relay: the per-device P-256 notification keypair and stable `device_uuid`, the per-host pinned sender-key set, registration against `POST /v1/notifications/register`, and the re-pin against `GET /v1/notifications/sender-keys`. Network cores (`register_impl`, `fetch_sender_keys_impl`) take an `&OAuthClient` and are tested against httpmock; the Keychain half is tested against the in-memory double, including the protection class each slot lands under
- `src-tauri/src/apns.rs` -- **iOS-only** APNs device-token bridge: installs the two `UIApplicationDelegate` token callbacks on Tauri's delegate class (add-only, never swizzle), requests notification authorization, and re-registers every managed identity when the token actually changes. Called once from `lib.rs`'s `setup`
- `src-tauri/Entitlements.ios.plist` -- the wallet's TRACKED iOS code-signing entitlements (iCloud Documents / ubiquity container for the blob backup, plus `aps-environment` for push — without which `registerForRemoteNotifications` never yields a token and the whole relay path is inert; like the iCloud container and UNLIKE `keychain-access-groups`, it needs the capability enabled on the App ID and the provisioning profile regenerated);

